            <ArticleTitle>Catalytic asymmetric Tamura cycloadditions involving nitroalkenes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1463-1474</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6ob02637k</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first examples of asymmetric Tamura cycloaddition reactions involving singly activated alkenes are reported. Homophthalic anhydride reacts with α-methyl nitrosytrenes in the presence of an alkaloid-based catalyst to generate fused bicyclic aromatic ketone products with three new stereocentres (which are susceptible to subsequent equilibration) in 12-99% ee. An unusual equilibration process which occurs in methanolic medium in the absence of a recognisable base via proton transfer at the α-carbon of an ester was investigated experimentally and computationally.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
